.TH Command REPAY
.SY "repay <LOAN>"
The repay command is used to repay loans from other countries.
.s3
The "<LOAN>" argument is the number of the loan you are repaying
and if not included on the command line it will be solicited by the program.
.s3
You can repay all or part of the loan with this command, however
beware of letting the loan become overdue -- the lender may
decide to force collection (see "info collect").
.s3
When you repay on a loan a telegram is sent to the lender
informing her/him of the amount repaid.
.s3
.EX repay 12
.NF
You presently owe $4515    payment : $2000
.FI
or,
.EX repay 12
.NF
You presently owe $4515   payment : $4515
Congratulations, you've paid off the loan!
.FI
.s3
See also : collect, consider, ledger, offer
